sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: VM CI (verifying-commands skill, "Run the same proof in development and CI"), docs/reference/feature-flow.md "The VM job", swamp/proof/reset/README.md, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof:run
  %% kind: proof.run
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant S as Proof VM<br/>task VM over ssh
  CLI->>GW: proof:run COMMIT
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit proof:run COMMIT`
  %%> - syntax: `<commit> [--all] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the full commit SHA and nothing else; Orbit selects the cases itself
  Note over GW: Check the commit<br/>branch head or approved PR
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node
  %%> - the SHA is a full lowercase SHA that the Orbit repository has
  %%> - the commit is the head of a branch of the Orbit repository
  %%> - or it is the head of an open pull request from elsewhere that carries the label `run-proofs` and has an approving review of exactly that commit from a maintainer
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a pull request from outside can carry any code; Orbit runs it only after a maintainer approved that exact commit
  %%> - the Gateway reads GitHub with its App token and fetches no code here
  Note over GW: Select the cases<br/>diff · selection list
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - lists the files that differ between the commit and its merge base with `main`
  %%> - maps each path with the selection list of the commit; the last matching line wins
  %%> - selects every case when the selection list changed or the file list is incomplete
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the selected case programs, and the paths that no case covers
  alt refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>proof.commit_untrusted
    %%> When:
    %%> - the commit is not trusted (`proof.commit_untrusted`) or unknown (`proof.commit_not_found`)
    %%> - a changed path matches no line of the selection list (`proof.path_unmapped`)
    %%> - the calling Node has no access grant (`node_access.required`)
    %%> - GitHub cannot be read, so the commit or its diff cannot be checked (`proof.github_unavailable`)
    %%> - the selection list is malformed (`proof.selection_invalid`)
    %%> - cases are selected and proof execution is switched off (`proof.execution_disabled`): the error holds the selected cases and the uncovered paths
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded and nothing starts
  else nothing to prove
    GW-->>CLI: Skipped — nothing to prove<br/>proof.nothing_to_prove
    %%> Result:
    %%> - only paths that need no proof changed, such as documentation and charts
    %%> - no VM is taken and nothing runs
    %%> - the task is recorded as succeeded, with no run
    %%> - paths marked as having no case yet are listed in the result
  else cases selected
    Note over GW: Record the task<br/>queue for a proof VM
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    Note over GW: Take a proof VM<br/>wait up to 10 min
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - a VM is free for the proof; one SQLite transaction takes it, so two runs never get the same one
    %%> When it waits:
    %%> - no VM is free: the task waits (`capacity`) and starts when a VM is released
    %%> - after the wait the task fails with `proof.no_vm`; nothing has started
    %%> Credential:
    %%> - the Gateway mints a short-lived, read-only GitHub token and pushes it to the vault under a key name
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-proof-run
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the commit, the selected case programs and the paths no case covers
    %%> - the VM name, host and image fingerprint
    %%> - the vault key name of the token, never its value
    SW->>S: Claim the VM<br/>child workflow · proof mode
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the shared claim phases: clone the topology seed, create the VM, start it, check it
    %%> Proof mode:
    %%> - the VM gets no Pi token, no model key and no real-fleet key
    %%> - the VM has no route to the real Gateway or to other Nodes
    SW->>S: Send the commit<br/>git bundle · ssh
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - Swamp fetches the commit with the vault token and sends only the new commits to the checkout in the VM
    %%> - the checkout ends clean at the exact commit
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the VM holds code, never a token
    SW->>S: Reset the test fleet<br/>proof-fleet-reset
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - boots the three ready nested VMs (Gateway with Swamp, `app-dev`, `app-prod`) from the snapshot
    %%> - applies the commit, joins the VM as the operator, and waits for fresh agent facts
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - no case runs; all selected cases end `unrun`
    SW->>S: Run the cases<br/>proof-command-verification
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs each selected case program in order against the fleet, with the real CLI built from the commit
    %%> - a case exits 0 (passed), 1 (failed) or 2 (unrun) and removes what it created
    %%> - compares the state each case touched with its state before the case; leftovers fail the case
    %%> - a case that needs a clean fleet gets a new reset
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - a command without a case program runs nothing and is listed as uncovered
    SW->>S: Copy the receipt<br/>ssh · evidence
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - copies case results, observations, Doctor findings, timings and run references to the receipt store, without secrets
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, also after a failure
    SW->>S: Release the VM<br/>child workflow
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - releases the nested fleet, deletes the VM and its seed clone
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, after the receipt is copied
    Note over SW: Check the verdicts<br/>assert
    %%> End check:
    %%> - every selected case has a verdict `passed`
    alt every case passes
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Record result<br/>verdicts · receipt link
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the task succeeds
      %%> - the result lists each case, the uncovered paths and the receipt link
    else a case fails or the fleet is not ready
      S--xSW: case fails or exit ≠ 0
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, verdicts
      Note over GW: Record the verdicts<br/>task fails
      %%> Result:
      %%> - `proof.cases_failed` when a case failed or did not run
      %%> - `proof.run_failed` when the fleet never became ready: every selected case is `unrun`
      %%> - each case is `passed`, `failed` or `unrun`; the receipt keeps the failed assertion and the command output
      %%> On the VM:
      %%> - the fleet and the VM are released also after a failure; only the receipt remains
      %%> - if the release fails, the failure shows in the operation
      %%> - the verdicts stay as they are
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the command again after the fix; it is a new run
    end
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
